# Project: WiFi CSI Human Activity Recognition Lab

Build a complete, Docker-first research platform for collecting synchronized WiFi CSI + camera data, automatically labeling activities from video, preprocessing CSI into ML-ready datasets, training CSI-based HAR models, and evaluating/inferencing those models.

The system must be operated primarily through a **web interface**.

The hardware is based on Espressif ESP32 devices and the official:

`espressif/esp-csi`

repository, specifically the `examples/get-started/csi_send` and `csi_recv` projects.

The CSI sender/receiver setup already works and produces approximately **100 CSI packets per second**.

Do not replace this working CSI acquisition approach unless there is a strong technical reason.

---

# 1. High-level objective

The final pipeline is:

```text
ESP32 CSI sender
        │
        ├──────── WiFi / ESP-NOW ─────────┐
        │                                 │
        ↓                                 ↓
 ESP32 receiver 1                  ESP32 receiver N
        │                                 │
        └──────── USB serial ─────────────┘
                         │
                         ↓
                 Docker host
                         │
             ┌───────────┴────────────┐
             │                        │
          CSI reader              USB camera
             │                        │
             └───────────┬────────────┘
                         ↓
             synchronized recording
                         │
                RAW SESSION DATA
                         │
         ┌───────────────┴───────────────┐
         │                               │
         ↓                               ↓
     raw CSI                         video.mp4
                                         │
                                         ↓
                              Video labeling model
                                         │
                                         ↓
                            timestamp activity labels
                                         │
                                         ↓
                               CSI preprocessing
                                         │
                                         ↓
                              windowed CSI dataset
                                         │
                                         ↓
                                CSI HAR model
                                         │
                                         ↓
                           activity classification
```

Target activities initially:

```text
empty_room
stand_still
sit_still
walking
fall
lying_still
```

Also support internal labels:

```text
unknown
transition
```

`fall` and `lying_still` MUST be separate classes.

A fall represents the actual falling event.

Do not label the entire period of a person lying on the floor as `fall`.

