# 22. CSI I/Q parsing

Espressif CSI raw bytes use interleaved imaginary/real values.

The parser must explicitly document and test this.

Convert the raw representation during preprocessing to a canonical:

```text
I/Q
```

representation.

Do not assume a hard-coded number of subcarriers such as 56.

Determine the usable CSI structure from:

```text
firmware configuration
CSI length
PHY configuration
selected LTFs
```

Record exactly which subcarriers were retained.

---

