# 24. Synchronization

The synchronization system must preserve several references:

```text
host_timestamp_ns
ESP local timestamp
tx_seq
video frame timestamp
```

Primary cross-modality synchronization:

```text
host monotonic timestamp
```

Primary synchronization between multiple CSI receivers:

```text
tx_seq
```

Retain the host timestamps too.

Do not assume packets always arrive without loss.

---

# 25. Collection startup synchronization

When recording starts:

1. Generate the session.
2. Initialize files.
3. Open selected serial devices.
4. Open camera.
5. Wait until hardware is ready.
6. Establish a shared monotonic start timestamp.
7. Begin CSI/video acquisition.
8. Record actual start timestamps.

Do not merely assume that subprocess launch time equals recording start time.

---

# 26. Collection shutdown

When Stop is pressed:

1. Stop accepting new frames/packets.
2. Flush CSI streams.
3. finalize video.
4. finalize timestamp Parquet file.
5. calculate statistics.
6. update metadata.
7. close all hardware handles.
8. mark session complete.

A crashed/incomplete session should be marked:

```text
incomplete
```

rather than silently appearing valid.

